From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:45:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-spm-sleep: end SODI idle periods 2 ms
 before the next timer

The idle state ended each period 5 ms before the next local timer event,
an interim value. Measured over 2404 timer-only wakes, the time from the
PCM timer's programmed end to CPU0 back in the idle path was 1.5-1.7 ms
and at most 1682 us, unpinned and with CPU0 pinned at 221 MHz alike. The
extra 3.3 ms left CPU0 in WFI after every timer wake, refused as "timer
due".

Set the exit latency to 2000 us, which also ends each period 2 ms before
the next event.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
index dfad504f9..814b7ef0e 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
@@ -1954,10 +1954,14 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(sodi_idle_disp_mask, "SODI idle: ignore the display's DRAM requ
 /*
  * The idle state with CPU0 powered down: the firmware saves and restores the
  * GIC on each side, so entry and exit cost far more than the WFI numbers
- * above. Deliberately conservative until measured (D7a): enter only for 20 ms
- * or more, and end the period 5 ms before the next local timer event.
+ * above. From a PCM-timer wake to CPU0 back in the idle path took 1.5-1.7 ms
+ * (1682 us at most) at every OPP, 221 MHz included, leaving DRAM self-refresh
+ * in most periods, with 26 MHz kept on (sodi_keep_26m): without it the exit
+ * adds the oscillator's settling and must be measured again. End the period
+ * 2 ms before the next local timer event. The 20 ms floor stays until a current
+ * reading shows shorter periods pay.
  */
-#define SODI_PDN_EXIT_US	5000
+#define SODI_PDN_EXIT_US	2000
 #define SODI_PDN_MIN_US		20000
 
